/-- **TIPD118 is exponentially stable for every `C9 ∈ [1 aF, 10 µF]`**, with `R4 = 8.2 Ω`: for
every rational `C ∈ [10⁻¹⁸, 10⁻⁵]` (in farads), the netlist read from `tipdText`
(`tipdText_parse`) with the capacitance of `C9` set to `C` is well formed, its operating point is
a trajectory, every differential state starts a trajectory, and every trajectory with zero input
converges to the operating point at the rate `9 s⁻¹` in all node potentials and branch currents.
This contains SLAU518's range `C9 ≤ 100 nF` (§2.1, p. 3) down to `1 aF`. -/
theorem tipd_range : tipdRangeCert.Guarantee tipdParsed.netlist :=
  CapacitanceRangeCert.guarantee_of_check tipdRangeCert_check

